      },
      "message": "fix(ui): show a progress overlay over the viewport while a toolpath generates\n\nIn the interactive window GenerateOperation now runs on a worker thread.\nThe world reads stay on the UI thread (StagedGeneration, the M5.3 B\nstaging seam made public); the generator, verification and stamp run on\nthe worker, and the result lands through the same undoable command.\n\n- The overlay names the operation, counts \"n of m\" when more wait,\n  shows the elapsed time and an activity bar, and has a Cancel button.\n- A result whose operation or cached path changed since staging is\n  discarded by name (GenerateOperation::still_current).\n- New and Open drop a running generation.\n- Tests, headless runs, scripts and MCP keep the synchronous path;\n  settle() waits for the worker.\n- The viewport takes no press inside the overlay.\n\nFixes #2257\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
